{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Analytic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.not_riemannHypothesis_const_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.not_riemannHypothesis_const_zero","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L166-L177","doc":"The second refuting witness: RH fails for the identically-zero\ncandidate, since `s = 1/4` lies in the strip and is a zero.\n\nTogether with `riemannHypothesis_const_one` this shows\n`RiemannHypothesis` is not constant in `ζ`, which is exactly why an\n`Iff` against an independently-quantified proposition proved `False`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.riemannHypothesis_const_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.riemannHypothesis_const_one","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L159-L164","doc":"The removed axiom's first refuting witness: RH holds vacuously for a\nnowhere-zero candidate. Kept so the inconsistency argument above is\ncheckable in this file rather than only in the commentary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.macroscopic_stability_equivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.macroscopic_stability_equivalence","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L149-L157","doc":"**Macroscopic stability equivalence, conditional on the conjecture.**\n\nDerives the third equivalence (1) ↔ (3) — the one the class does *not*\ncarry — by transitivity. This is a derivation from the hypotheses, not\na projection of a field (§3b-cond item 5). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:macroscopic-stability-equivalence","label":"conj:macroscopic-stability-equivalence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence.rh_iff_critical_line","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence.rh_iff_critical_line","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L147-L147","doc":"(2) ↔ (3): RH ↔ the Reeb spectrum of this datum on the critical line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence.stability_iff_rh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence.stability_iff_rh","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L145-L145","doc":"(1) ↔ (2): optimal Chebyshev error ↔ RH, for this datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStabilityEquivalence","kind":"class","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L127-L147","doc":"**Primary conjecture (open — no instance is provided, and none should\nbe added without a proof).**\n\nFor one substrate datum, macroscopic stability, the Riemann hypothesis\nfor that datum's zeta function, and critical-line behaviour of that\ndatum's Reeb spectrum are pairwise equivalent.\n\nField 1 is classical in one direction (von Koch 1901: RH implies the\noptimal Chebyshev error; the converse follows from the explicit\nformula) but is not available in Mathlib. Field 2 is the framework's\nown claim and is entirely open.\n\nBoth fields quantify over the *same* `D`, so neither forces either side\nto be constant in its argument — the equivalence is between two\nproperties of one system, which is what the informal statement always\nmeant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum.rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum.rho","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L125-L125","doc":"Reeb eigenvalues, indexed by deformation level and by the eight\ngenerators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum.psi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum.psi","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L122-L122","doc":"The associated Chebyshev-type prime-counting function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum.zeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum.zeta","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L120-L120","doc":"The candidate zeta function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L118-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateSpectralDatum","kind":"structure","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L112-L125","doc":"One system: a candidate zeta function, its Chebyshev-type counting\nfunction, and the Reeb spectrum of the same substrate.\n\nThe three fields exist to be related to **each other**. Quantifying\nover them independently is precisely the defect that made the removed\naxioms inconsistent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CriticalLineSpectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CriticalLineSpectrum","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L102-L110","doc":"Critical-line behaviour of the Reeb spectrum: every eigenvalue, at\nevery deformation level, has real part `1/2`.\n\nThis is the statement the removed `SpectralPersistence` was meant to\nmake. That version quantified over all levels in its hypothesis and\nconcluded about level `0` only, which is instantiation and is provable\noutright; this one has content because it constrains the family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MacroscopicStability","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L93-L100","doc":"Macroscopic stability: the Chebyshev-type function `ψ` satisfies\n`ψ(X) = X + O(X^{1/2+ε})` for every `ε > 0`.\n\nStated over `ℝ`: the ordering, `|·|` and `rpow` are archimedean, so\nthis sits on the archimedean side of the wall by necessity (§7c). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RiemannHypothesis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.RiemannHypothesis","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/macroscopic-stability-equivalence.lean#L88-L91","doc":"Riemann hypothesis for a given candidate zeta function: every zero in\nthe critical strip lies on the critical line. ","signatureChunk":0}]}